{
  "sources": [
    {
      "source_id": "ae-en-shutter-latch-doc",
      "version": "1",
      "language": "en",
      "family_id": "ae-en-shutter-latch",
      "text": "Claim 1. A folding shutter with a frame under a stone lintel and a draw latch.\n\nClaim 2. The folding shutter of claim 1 configured for the quarry application.\n\nClaim 3. The folding shutter of claim 2, wherein the draw latch has a keeper in the form of a hooked tab.\n\nClaim 4. A folding shutter for the orchard application, with a frame under a stone lintel and a draw latch having a keeper in the form of a hooked tab.\n\nClaim 5. The folding shutter of claim 4, including a locator notch on the frame.\n\nClaim 6. A folding shutter for the mill application, with a frame under a timber lintel and a draw latch having a keeper in the form of a flat plate.\n",
      "sha256": "4642358fbd6233b4142f3b5f63d4cbd23fffa2c2f7ca32d76c4140dcd1caf15b"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "ae-en-map-cabinet-doc",
      "version": "1",
      "language": "en",
      "family_id": "ae-en-map-cabinet",
      "text": "[12] In the wall unit, the drawing drawer uses a stop described under [13]. The wall unit takes a shallow drawer.\n\n[13] The stop for the drawer is a cork pad secured to the rear rail.\n\n[21] In the bench unit, the shallow drawer has the stop called out in drawing note D.\n\nNote D. Stop at the inner end of the runner: cork pad.\n\nNote F. The feet carry a maker's stamp.\n",
      "sha256": "4aaaa11cfa2b33a94ae2e7fb43cfbd48d5659d6f9f3cd56d92e8c906020e9aca"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "ae-en-tile-rack-doc",
      "version": "Amber",
      "language": "en",
      "family_id": "ae-en-tile-rack",
      "text": "Section 2. This specification covers the indoor rack.\n\nSection 5. Issue Amber specifies a birch board for each shelf in the installation specified in section 2.\n",
      "sha256": "adc9c787f0cebd188eba1fbef4d1b59d9de1ca58e8738ccc119962946acb8659"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "ae-en-tile-rack-doc",
      "version": "Slate",
      "language": "en",
      "family_id": "ae-en-tile-rack",
      "text": "Section 5. Issue Slate replaces section 5 of Issue Amber. Retain the scope defined in section 2 of Issue Amber. Use the shelf stock shown at note S.\n\nNote S. Shelf stock for this issue: glazed clay slab.\n\nSection 7. Fit the shop badge to the outside edge.\n",
      "sha256": "2cb04d66137e2e81214ac3f7d6dab5cc6a35519477f54b0df425b4b58015b529"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "ae-en-spindle-gauge-doc",
      "version": "1",
      "language": "en",
      "family_id": "ae-en-spindle-gauge",
      "text": "Section 8. For the guide spindle, use the shaft diameter given in dimension callout B.\n\nDimension callout B. Shaft diameter: six millimetres.\n\nSection 9. The handle sits above the plate.\n\nDimension callout H. Plate width: forty millimetres.\n",
      "sha256": "bcbfa99de28ca2bcf8c9db25980abd9ec661ac9249777034653d1becfb341ffa"
    }
  ],
